From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 05:50:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] toml: let expand() make the first allocation

eg25-manager aborts on startup on every device and with every config file:

    Opening config file: /usr/share/eg25-manager/pine64,pinephone-pro.toml
    unable to parse config file: out of memory
    eg25-manager.service: Main process exited, code=dumped, status=6/ABRT

The config is not at fault - an empty file fails identically, and the
shipped ones parse fine with a standards-compliant parser.

toml_parse_file() starts with an empty buffer and grows it:

    int   bufsz = 0;
    char *buf   = 0;
    while (!feof(fp)) {
        if (off == bufsz) {
            int   xsz = bufsz + 1000;
            char *x = expand(buf, bufsz, xsz);
            if (!x) {
                snprintf(errbuf, errbufsz, "out of memory");

so the very first expand() is always called with p == NULL. Commit
f978b77 ("src: fix issues reported by clang-tidy") added

    if (!p)
        return 0;

to the top of expand(), presumably to avoid memcpy(s, NULL, 0), which is
undefined behaviour even for a zero length. But expand() is the allocator
here, not just a grower: returning early on a NULL input means the buffer
is never allocated at all, toml_parse_file() reports "out of memory" and
g_error() aborts the process. No config file can ever be read.

Keep the intent - never memcpy from NULL - but allocate first and only
copy when there is something to copy.

Without this the modem is never powered on, so ofono comes up with no
device:

    msm-modem-uim-selection.sh: Waited 45 seconds for modem device to appear
    msm-modem-uim-selection.sh: 2 No modem available.
    ofonod: create_rilmodem: ofono_modem_register returned: -19

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
---
 src/toml.c | 10 +++++-----
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

--- a/src/toml.c
+++ b/src/toml.c
@@ -397,15 +397,15 @@
 static void *expand(void *p, int sz, int newsz)
 {
     void *s;
-    if (!p)
-        return 0;
 
     s = MALLOC(newsz);
     if (!s)
         return 0;
 
-    memcpy(s, p, sz);
-    FREE(p);
+    if (p) {
+        memcpy(s, p, sz);
+        FREE(p);
+    }
     return s;
 }
 
